        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Martin Heidegger, Lytton Strachey\n- Concepts: Thrownness, philosophical hermeneutics, Continental tradition\n- Roles: philosopher, writer, critic\n\nFacts:\n- Giles Lytton Strachey was born on 1 March 1880 and died on 21 January 1932.\n- Martin Heidegger was born on 26 September 1889 and died on 26 May 1976.\n- Lytton Strachey was a British writer and critic.\n- Martin Heidegger was a German philosopher and a seminal thinker in the Continental tradition and philosophical hermeneutics.\n- Thrownness, or \"Geworfenheit,\" is a concept introduced by Martin Heidegger to describe human existence as being thrown into the world.",
